own_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"case_numbers":["2024-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Kevin Bigelow complained against multiple actions of North Florida Presbytery related to the dissolution of his call as Assistant Pastor of Christ Church East (where he was also serving as planting pastor at Christ Church Beaches). The SJC sustained the complaint in part (22-0-0), finding that Presbytery erred in…"}},{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Gordon v. Southern New England Presbytery","year":2022,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md:occ-6398e2d939e9","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.html","repository_path":"cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":291},"excerpt":"…5 was revised again, including the addition of what is now BCO 5-5. In 2015, BCO 5-2 was revised, and the last revision to BCO Chapter 5 came in 2017 with a revision to 5-3. Thus, it is difficult to argue that BCO 13-8 supersedes or stands in place of the…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga49_2022__2020-06.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["church transfer between denominations","OPC to PCA membership transfer","excommunication","jurisdiction","membership vows","failure to attend worship","session authority limits"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2020-6"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"A church member appealed Presbytery’s affirmance of his conviction and excommunication for failing to heed Session admonition and membership vows, including prolonged absence from that church. The SJC affirmed and denied the appeal, holding that all four specifications—lack of reasonable indulgence, haste, prejudice, and injustice—were nonspecific and unsupported. It emphasized his admissions that the charges were true, the adequate timeline, and the bar on considering evidence not offered at trial. A dissent disputed his PCA membership, standing, and the Session’s jurisdiction."}},{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"the Session of Hope Community Church v. Central Carolina Presbytery","year":2014,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md:occ-1b789cfe9adc","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":75},"excerpt":"…it as such, Presbytery's Manual imposes a requirement which does not appear in BCO 5-2 or 5-3b. The imposition of such a requirement violates the judgment and discretion afforded the Session to determine the extent of its participatory role in the creation…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md"},{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md:occ-ebbb9e6c25b6","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":75},"excerpt":"…a Session may play in the initiation and oversight of mission churches. (See BCO 5-2 and 5-3b). While the new worship location in this case does not function as a separate mission church, to the extent Presbytery's Manual requires the local Session to…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga42_2014__2013-04.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["multi-site church","particularization","session authority over time and place of worship","presbytery manual","church planting policy","mission church","presbytery limits on session authority","BCO vs. presbytery rules"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2013-4"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Hope Community Church’s Session challenged Presbytery’s requirement that a multi-site congregation eventually particularize its second worship site. The SJC sustained the complaint, annulled the requirement, and struck it from the Presbytery Manual because BCO 12-5e specifically entrusts the time and place of worship to the Session, which Presbytery’s general church-enlargement authority could not supersede. The narrow ruling did not resolve broader concerns about multi-site churches or eliminate Presbytery’s review of a second site’s location under BCO 13-9(g)."}},{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Smith v. Northeast Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:5-2--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md:occ-b9dc3efc30bd","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":198},"excerpt":"BCO 5-2 provides for \"oversight\" of a mission church by its presbytery.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-01.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["dissolved congregation","presbytery administrative commission","church membership","jurisdiction","complaint procedure","constitutional rights"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1993-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Smith complained that Northeast Presbytery failed to provide pastoral care after dissolving Grace Presbyterian Church. The SJC rejected Presbytery's objections that the complaint lacked supporting reasons or was barred by Smith's protest, held it in order, but denied it on the merits. Distinguishing the pastoral 'power of order' from judicial 'power of jurisdiction,' the SJC ruled that the Constitution neither requires nor permits a presbytery to retain jurisdiction over individual members of a dissolved particular church, and that pastoral care of former members is generally discretionary; on these facts, Presbytery's efforts satisfied any duty."}},{"id":"bco:5-2--overture:ga41_2013:2","record_id":"overture:ga41_2013:2","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 5-1, 5-2, 5-9 and Add Sections 5-11 and 5-12 Regarding Mission Churches","year":2013,"disposition":"Referred","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.